  // passes this array as `selects` to SSRPass — when selective SSR is on,
  // the metalness mask is rendered ONLY for these meshes, so reflections
  // appear on water surfaces and on aircraft skin, and nowhere else
  // (terrain, props stay un-SSR'd and don't pick up noisy artifacts).
  //
  // 机身材质: metalness .5/roughness .5 在**高角度太阳**(下午两点 52°)下会打出大片镜面
  // (用户: "机身变得这么光滑") ⇒ 改成 .42/.62, 保持哑光金属观感。
  // Aircraft: their MeshStandardMaterial uses metalness 0.5-0.7, which SSR
  // interprets as "reflective". By adding the player + enemy + wingman
  // fuselage meshes to this list, the SSR pass picks up sky/cloud/terrain
  // reflections on the aircraft skin — making fighters look like they're
  // really flying through the environment instead of being flat-shaded.
  private _ssrWaterMeshes: THREE.Mesh[] = [];
